      "id": "table-1",
      "line": 297,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Situation",
        "Do",
        "Because (this guide)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "designing a shared tool",
          "check the **work/benefit disparity**",
          "those who bear the cost won't sustain it (§1)"
        ],
        [
          "the tool is empty at launch",
          "deliver **single-user value first**",
          "beats the critical-mass chicken-and-egg (§6)"
        ],
        [
          "async / remote collaboration",
          "design for **grounding cost** (back-channels, history)",
          "lean media force grounding onto people (§3)"
        ],
        [
          "coordinating dependencies",
          "make **dependencies + handoffs** visible; don't kill articulation work",
          "rigid systems break on exceptions (§4)"
        ],
        [
          "coordinating turns/attention",
          "**social translucence** (visibility + mutual awareness)",
          "enables self-coordination without a rigid protocol (§5)"
        ],
        [
          "claiming a group benefit",
          "measure a **group/system outcome**",
          "individual SUS is necessary, not sufficient (§7)"
        ],
        [
          "claiming adoption/network effect",
          "study **multiple groups over time**",
          "one pilot's buzz proves nothing (§6)"
        ],
        [
          "evaluating collaboration",
          "**field study** (`06`); bound transfer",
          "a lab can't reproduce org rules or critical mass (§7)"
        ],
        [
          "an awareness feature feels like monitoring",
          "keep it **mutual + legitimate**; route legality to `law/`",
          "coordination, not surveillance (§2, `11`)"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}